WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.299
We all know John McAfee for one reason: McAfee’s
antivirus software.

00:00:05.299 --> 00:00:09.840
Though his antivirus software is what garnered
him worldwide fame, John was actually never

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.019
that proud of this creation.

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:17.830
For most of us, building a popular antivirus
software that Intel would buy for $7.7 billion

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.450
would be the highlight of our lives.

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:23.840
But for John McAfee who had racked up achievements
ranging from working on the Apollo program

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.300
to running for US president, his stint with
antivirus software was just another part of

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.480
his life.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:33.740
Unfortunately though, I’m sure all of you
guys heard about what just happened to John,

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.270
so here’s the bitter fall of John McAfee.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:44.850
John McAfee was born on September 18, 1945
on a US army base located in Cinderford, England.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:49.260
Though he was born in England, most of his
childhood would be spent in Salem Virginia.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.920
John didn’t have the greatest of childhoods
as his father was apparently an abusive alcoholic

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.260
who took his own life when John was 15 years
old.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.300
His father’s alcoholism rubbed off on John
as he picked up heavy drinking at a pretty

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.560
early age.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:06.550
Despite his heavy drinking though, John was
a high functioning alcoholic who didn’t

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.930
prevent his addiction from disrupting his
academic excellence.

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:14.890
McAfee would attend Roanoke College in Virginia
and earn his bachelors in mathematics in 1967.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:19.580
He would instantly turn around and pursue
a mathematics doctorate from Roanoke, but

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.240
this wouldn’t last too long.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.000
You see, during his doctorate studies, John
would form a relationship with an undergraduate

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.140
student that the school was not too fond of.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:33.740
The school would expel John for this relationship,
but John wasn’t too worried.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.490
He already ran a local door to door magazine
business which he says made him a small fortune.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.900
Moreover, he was able to land a job at Nasa
soon after being expelled in 1968.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:48.300
During his time at Nasa, John worked on the
Apollo program as a programmer, and though

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:52.800
he would only work at Nasa for 2 years, those
2 years happened to be 2 of the most important

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.060
years for Nasa as they would place humans
on the moon in 1969.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:00.870
After his time at Nasa, John would jump from
one company to another throughout the early

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:01.870
1970s.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:06.200
Throughout this time period, John woud transition
from simply being an alcoholic to being a

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.440
drug addict.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:11.810
John says that drug use was extremely common
within the tech industry at the time and that

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.390
most of his bosses used them as well.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.170
Apparently, he had to hide them from his mother
and wife, but he didn’t have to hide them

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.300
at the office during lunchtime.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.360
During this dark period of his life, he took
on various software developer roles at Univac,

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:29.250
Xerox, CSC, Booz Allen, and Lockheed.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:33.340
Though his career was progressing just fine,
his life was starting to fall apart.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:38.560
In the early 1980s, his first wife would leave
him and he would finally come to the realization

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.400
that he was too dependent on drugs and alcohol.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.230
So, he would join a rehabilitation organization
called Alcoholics Anonymous which would help

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.750
him quit in 1984.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.470
At the time, he was working at Lockheed when
the first computer virus called Brain came

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:53.470
out.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.130
Intrigued by the virus, John would start to
develop software that could combat computer

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.130
viruses.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:03.270
And, it wouldn’t take long for John to start
McAfee Associates in 1987 which sold the first

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.580
anti virus software on the market.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:09.570
In the late 1980s, the average person didn’t
have a computer though and the people who

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:13.110
did have a computer didn’t quite understand
the threat of viruses.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:18.490
So, selling antivirus software for $50 a piece
likely wouldn't have been that successful.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:22.989
John was well aware of this, and that’s
why he gave away his software for free.

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:26.860
The company made money from providing additional
technical support and upgrades.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:31.099
This clever move allowed the company to quickly
dominate the market as there was really no

00:03:31.099 --> 00:03:34.290
reason to not have McAfee antivirus software.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.210
Whether you thought computer viruses were
a serious threat or not, having extra protection

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.760
for free was a no brainer.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.170
As the software exploded in popularity, so
did the company’s revenue as they were making

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:48.069
$5 million per year by the end of the 1980s.

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:53.110
Going into the 1990s, the company’s popularity
would only continue to grow as computer viruses

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:55.069
became more prevalent.

00:03:55.069 --> 00:03:59.830
In 1992, a virus called Michelangelo would
make a grand debut infecting tens of thousands

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.129
of computers.

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:05.270
Though that scale is nothing compared to what
we see today, Michelangelo became a turning

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.580
point for consumer awareness surrounding computer
viruses.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:13.040
McAfee would leverage this newfound attention
and go public in 1992.

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:18.829
In 1993, John would reduce his role in the
company stepping down from CEO to CTO.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:23.789
John would actually leave the company altogether
the following year, but this didn’t really

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:24.789
matter.

00:04:24.789 --> 00:04:28.360
He had already built up McAfee to a strong
position, and all that was left was continuing

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:31.410
to improve their products and waiting for
the market to grow.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.490
But this is when John’s downfall would begin.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:40.390
He would go ahead and sell his entire stake
in McAfee which was worth $100 million at

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:41.390
the time.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:46.440
While that’s an awesome sum of money, McAfee
was still a very young company and internet/computer

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.969
adoption was just starting to ramp up.

00:04:48.969 --> 00:04:52.830
So, selling his entire stake was a pretty
stupid financial decision.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:56.620
That’s like selling your apple stake when
the iPhone 4 came out.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.249
Moreover, John didn’t even have to do anything.

00:04:59.249 --> 00:05:02.949
He just had to wait, and he would’ve become
a multi billionaire in no time.

00:05:02.949 --> 00:05:06.319
But alas, that’s not what happened.

00:05:06.319 --> 00:05:10.110
To make things even worse, he wouldn’t preserve
very much of the $100 million that he did

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:11.289
cash out.

00:05:11.289 --> 00:05:14.020
John would turn around and go on a shopping
spree.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:20.339
He would buy a $25 million mansion in Colorado,
a mansion in Hawaii, a private jet, a 157

00:05:20.339 --> 00:05:24.289
acre ranch in New Mexico, and dozens of luxury
cars.

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:28.279
He basically blew most of his money and put
the rest in Lehman Brothers bonds.

00:05:28.279 --> 00:05:32.620
Though this was a terrible financial decision,
he wouldn’t feel the impact of this decision

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.589
for quite some time.

00:05:34.589 --> 00:05:38.469
Throughout the late 1990s and early 2000s,
John would lecture at Stanford’s business

00:05:38.469 --> 00:05:42.930
school and work on two social network projects
called PowWow and Tribal Voice.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:46.249
Neither of these projects ever gained that
much traction though.

00:05:46.249 --> 00:05:50.490
Soon enough the financial crisis of 2008 would
roll around, and this would basically wipe

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:52.470
out the rest of John’s fortune.

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:56.360
The Lehman brothers would go bankrupt which
would make John’s bonds worthless.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:02.279
Meanwhile, he would have to sell his $25 million
Colorado mansion for just $5.7 million and

00:06:02.279 --> 00:06:05.849
his Hawaiin mansion would be sold for $1.5
million.

00:06:05.849 --> 00:06:10.180
Unfortunately, he basically sold at the bottom
of the market, and when everything was said

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.259
and done, he only had $4 million.

00:06:12.259 --> 00:06:16.419
While that’s still a decent amount, when
you consider that he was on the verge of making

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:20.360
$4 billion, it’s really just quite sad.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:25.000
Since he burned his fortune, John would move
to Belize in 2009 where his remaining $4 million

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.009
would stretch much further.

00:06:27.009 --> 00:06:31.150
While at Belize, McAfee would start a pharmaceutical
company called Quorumex.

00:06:31.150 --> 00:06:35.259
The company was supposed to use plants to
combat various illnesses, but this attracted

00:06:35.259 --> 00:06:37.449
a lot of attention from the authorities.

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:41.119
The police suspected that he was manufacturing
methamphetamine and they would raid his house

00:06:41.119 --> 00:06:42.930
in May of 2012.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:47.479
They wouldn’t find any methamphetamine,
but they did find an abundant amount of firearms

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:50.319
which provoked them to throw John in jail
for a night.

00:06:50.319 --> 00:06:54.839
Later that same year, one of McAfee’s neighbors
named Gregory Faull would be murdered.

00:06:54.839 --> 00:06:58.839
John would become the prime suspect due to
his large possession of firearms and his unfriendly

00:06:58.839 --> 00:06:59.839
relationship with Gregory.

00:06:59.839 --> 00:07:04.779
Gregory apparently poisoned John’s dogs,
and this is the alleged reason for John wanting

00:07:04.779 --> 00:07:06.439
to take out Gregory.

00:07:06.439 --> 00:07:09.710
But none of these allegations were ever confirmed.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:13.650
John would claim that the Belizian authorities
were trying to frame him and he would flee

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:14.650
to Guatemala.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:19.180
Unfortunately for John, a Vice reporter would
accidentally leak his location and Guatemalan

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.710
authorities would arrest him for illegally
entering the country and they would deport

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.650
him back to the US.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:29.990
After returning to the US in 2013, John would
start to flame McAfee Antivirus Software claiming

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:33.659
that it had become one of the worst products
on the planet.

00:07:33.659 --> 00:07:37.619
He didn’t like that his name was still being
used to market the product, and when Intel

00:07:37.619 --> 00:07:41.590
announced that they would change the branding
of McAfee to Intel security, John expressed

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.930
that he was eternally grateful to Intel.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:49.369
Ironically, McAfee would end up demerging
with Intel in 2017 and take on the name McAfee

00:07:49.369 --> 00:07:50.569
once again.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:56.490
The demerged company actually just went public
at the end of 2020, and they’re worth about

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.490
$12 billion today.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.599
Clearly, McAfee corporation has been consistently
growing, but the same cannot be said about

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:02.599
John.

00:08:02.599 --> 00:08:05.900
After returning to the US in 2013, his life
just became even sketchier.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:10.909
In 2016, he was appointed as the CEO of MGT
Capital Investments.

00:08:10.909 --> 00:08:15.349
The company was originally focused on investing
into social gaming companies, but John would

00:08:15.349 --> 00:08:17.289
change the focus to cybersecurity.

00:08:17.289 --> 00:08:22.309
Specifically, John wanted to leverage cryptocurrencies
and blockchain technology to improve cyber

00:08:22.309 --> 00:08:23.309
security.

00:08:23.309 --> 00:08:27.409
I think a lot of us would agree that this
is an awesome idea, as blockchain technology

00:08:27.409 --> 00:08:30.179
does seem to be the future of cyber security.

00:08:30.179 --> 00:08:34.630
But, at the same time, John was also involved
in pumping and dumping cryptos.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:40.490
Between December 2017 and October 2018, John
would recommend cryptos such as Reddcoin and

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.470
Dogecoin to his twitter followers.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:46.930
He would then go on to sell his own holdings
after the prices of these cryptos were inflated.

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.160
This practice would eventually get him charged
for securities fraud.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.960
John entered the crypto space decently early,
and I think he could’ve built something

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:58.680
rather large if he put his mind to it, but
unfortunately, he chose to spend his time

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.090
pumping and dumping meme coins.

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:05.160
And that brings us into his final activity
which would seal his fate.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:10.360
In 2019, John revealed that he hadn’t filed
taxes since 2010 citing that taxation was

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.090
against the constitution.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:17.050
He even tried to remove taxation by trying
to become president in 2016 and 2020.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.980
In 2016, he originally ran as a candidate
of the newly formed Cyber Party, but he would

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:25.600
eventually switch over to the libertarian
party.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.190
Though he didn’t win the nomination, he
actually did pretty well.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:33.430
He placed second in the primaries and third
in the Libertarian National Convention.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:38.150
In 2020 though, his bid for presidency wasn’t
nearly as viable as he was being chased by

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:39.830
the IRS for tax evasion.

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:45.150
Eventually, the authorities would catch up
to him, arresting him on October 5, 2020.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.590
At this point, he was basically screwed.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:51.710
His decade of tax evasion had earned him up
to 30 years in prison meaning that he would

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.550
likely spend the rest of his life in prison.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:10:00.160
On June 23, 2021, his extradition to the US
would be approved and a few hours later he

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:03.710
would be found dead in his prison cell seemingly
due to suicide.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:10.370
His wife says that he wasn’t suicidal and
in 2019 McAfee tweeted quote “If I suicide

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:13.080
myself, I didn’t, I was whackd.”

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:17.460
Considering this, his wife is seeking a thorough
investigation into his death.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:21.820
Unfortunately though, this is likely one of
those cases where we will never figure out

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.130
what happened.

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:27.750
What we know for sure, however, is that John
McAfee was a pioneer in cybersecurity and

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:31.760
we all use bits and parts of his original
technology today.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.610
What do you guys think was the turning point
in McAfee’s life?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.970
Comment that down below.

00:10:35.970 --> 00:10:40.750
Also, drop a like if you think that McAfee
deserves a fair and thorough investigation.

